#: ../../source/docs/rover-sitlmavproxy-tutorial.rst:7
#: e5f9aaba358f4b53a4126521511ca593
msgid "This tutorial provides a basic walk-through of how to use :ref:`SITL <sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop>` and :ref:`MAVProxy<mavproxy:home>` for *Rover* testing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-sitlmavproxy-tutorial.rst:12
#: 9146ea14dd624cb7b567b7dbe7990f93
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-sitlmavproxy-tutorial.rst:14
#: fcfa9839448645588fb51b85f4196571
msgid "Rover is an easy platform to get started with. Unlike Copter or Plane there are no fast-moving propellers, so there is no need to arm motors. As movement is along the ground, there is no need to consider taking off or landing, and pausing/loitering/waiting is just \"stopping\". At the end of initialization the Rover is ready to go!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-sitlmavproxy-tutorial.rst:20
#: 218e28779c1c4be28bf21a9fb7c2f781
msgid "The article is intended primarily for developers who want to test new Rover builds and bug fixes using SITL and *MAVProxy*. It shows how to use the different modes, run missions, set a geofence, and perform a number of other basic testing tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-sitlmavproxy-tutorial.rst:25
#: 64daed24c60f4bc29c77bd5b2def05c0
msgid "The tutorial is complementary to the topic :ref:`Using SITL for ArduPilot Testing <using-sitl-for-ardupilot-testing>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-sitlmavproxy-tutorial.rst:29
#: 78c7b9810ffd49cda943a50eaab970ee
msgid "We use *MAVProxy* here, but you can :ref:`attach another ground station to SITL <using-sitl-for-ardupilot-testing_connecting_otheradditional_ground_stations>` if you prefer (similar instructions can be used in any GCS)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-sitlmavproxy-tutorial.rst:31
#: 79732637328547a6aecfef80a4848364
msgid "This tutorial is for Rover - see :ref:`Copter <copter-sitl-mavproxy-tutorial>` and :ref:`Plane <plane-sitlmavproxy-tutorial>` for similar tutorials on the other vehicles."
